{#
    Breadcrumbs + back button of the pages that live inside something (docs/features/xp-levels/ux-polish/design-spec.md §3):
    one row - a round ‹ back button, then the trail of PARENTS (the H1 is the current page, as on the event pages).

    Variables:
      levels    list<{name, label?, url}> the parents, outermost first. name = full text (JSON-LD, accessible names),
                label = optional shorter visible text. [] = no trail.
      current   the current page's name - only the last ListItem of the JSON-LD (no `item`, Google's rule).
      json_ld   (default false) emit the BreadcrumbList JSON-LD. Only on public, indexable pages.
      back      (optional) {name, url} where the back button goes without `?return=`. Default = the last level.
                For pages whose trail is something else - the owner pages, where the compact player strip is the
                trail: `levels: [], back: {name: player name, url: path('player_profile', …)}` plus the strip in
                the `trail` block (embed). See templates/xp_history.html.twig.

    The back button goes to the real previous place: a valid `?return=` (safe_return_url() - never off-site), labelled
    with `?return_title=`; otherwise `back`, otherwise the last level. A `?return=` that is the page we just came from
    is a history.back() (page_back_controller.js, design-spec §8.7) - a plain link without JS. No levels, no `back` and no valid `?return=` =
    nothing is rendered (also no JSON-LD: a page without parents has no trail to describe).

    Usage:
      {{ include('_page_crumbs.html.twig', {levels: [{name: 'progression_hub.title'|trans, url: path('progression_hub')}],
          current: 'xp.explainer.title'|trans, json_ld: true}) }}
      Back button only (pages without a trail - leaderboards, player pages): {{ include('_page_crumbs.html.twig', {levels: []}) }}
      Own trail markup next to the button: {% embed '_page_crumbs.html.twig' with {levels: [], back: …} %}{% block trail %}…{% endblock %}{% endembed %}

    Links that bring people here with `?return=` are rel="nofollow"; the canonical URL never carries it (base.html.twig).
    Styles: assets/styles/_page-crumbs.scss
#}
{%- set levels = levels|default([]) -%}
{%- set last_level = levels is empty ? null : levels|last -%}
{%- set back_default = back is defined and back is not null ? back : last_level -%}
{%- set return_url = safe_return_url(app.request.query.get('return')) -%}
{%- if return_url is not null -%}
    {%- set back_url = return_url -%}
    {%- set back_title = app.request.query.get('return_title')|default('')|trim|slice(0, 80) -%}
{%- elseif back_default is not null -%}
    {%- set back_url = back_default.url -%}
    {%- set back_title = back_default.name -%}
{%- else -%}
    {%- set back_url = null -%}
    {%- set back_title = '' -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- set back_label = back_title != '' ? 'page_crumbs.back_to'|trans({'%title%': back_title}) : 'page_crumbs.back'|trans -%}

{%- if back_url is not null or levels is not empty %}
<div class="page-crumbs{{ levels|length > 2 ? ' page-crumbs-long' }}">
    {%- if back_url is not null %}
    <a class="page-crumbs-back" href="{{ back_url }}" aria-label="{{ back_label }}" title="{{ back_label }}"
        {%- if return_url is not null %} {{ stimulus_controller('page-back') }} {{ stimulus_action('page-back', 'back') }}{% endif %}><i class="bi bi-chevron-left" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- block trail %}
    {%- if levels is not empty %}
    <nav class="page-crumbs-trail" aria-label="{{ 'page_crumbs.label'|trans }}">
        <ol>
            {%- for level in levels %}
            {%- if loop.index == 2 and loop.length > 2 %}
            <li class="page-crumbs-fold" aria-hidden="true">…</li>
            {%- endif %}
            <li{% if not loop.first and not loop.last %} class="page-crumbs-middle"{% endif %}><a href="{{ level.url }}"{% if (level.label ?? level.name) != level.name %} title="{{ level.name }}"{% endif %}>{{ level.label ?? level.name }}</a></li>
            {%- endfor %}
        </ol>
    </nav>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- endblock %}
</div>
{%- if json_ld|default(false) and levels is not empty %}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
        {%- for level in levels %}
        {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": {{ loop.index }},
            "name": {{ level.name|json_ld }},
            "item": {{ absolute_url(level.url)|json_ld }}
        },
        {%- endfor %}
        {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": {{ levels|length + 1 }},
            "name": {{ current|default('')|json_ld }}
        }
    ]
}
</script>
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
